  <reporting-org ref="GB-CHC-285776" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">CAFOD</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Civil Society Development consultancy</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;	To undertake preliminary discussions with the Joint Tr&#xf3;caire/CAFOD team in Addis Ababa on the scope of the emerging Civil Society Development Programme - helping us take stock of where we&apos;ve come from, and take a critical look at the future, helping the Team move from &apos;organic&apos; to &apos;intentional&apos; mode: this includes helping the team to sharpen the Programme Proposal Document and to identify longer term strategies and impact indicators, and the ways and means of monitoring these.
&quot;	To participate in a team discussion about the EC Civil Society Call for Proposals (scheduled for May). The emphasis of this call is on international NGOs assisting the building of capacities of the Ethiopian NGOs to be able to apply for EC funds when the next Call is made. You will help the Joint Team to think through options for developing a proposal to submit by July and, if appropriate, may help in the development of that proposal.
&quot;	In support of this, you will undertake some focused interviews with key Addis-based reps of partners and a few telephone interviews with partners outside Addis, which will provide useful input into the proposal development. It is possible that a 1.5 day trip to Tigray may be undertaken.
&quot;	To help the Joint team consider its own capacity needs as the Civil Society Programme grows. It is currently over dependent on the resources of the Joint Country Representatives - but it is not easy to see exactly what kinds of additional capacity would enrich rather than over-complicate the Team.</narrative>
  </description>
